An outlier is a number that is very different from all the other numbers.

or

An outlier is a value that is much bigger or much smaller than all the other values.

Think of it as the odd one out.

=========

The odd one out" in a group of numbers. That's exactly what your preprocessing task is trying to find before using the data for analysis or machine learning.

========

Daily Ice Cream Sales

A shop sells:

| Day       | Ice Creams Sold |
| --------- | --------------: |
| Monday    |              20 |
| Tuesday   |              22 |
| Wednesday |              19 |
| Thursday  |              21 |
| Friday    |              20 |
| Saturday  |         **500** |

Selling 500 on one day while all other days are around 20 is unusual.

🍦 500 is an outlier.

