============

Imagine you are the class teacher and you ask all students to write their exam marks.

| Student |   Marks |
| ------- | ------: |
| Arun    |      78 |
| Bala    |      82 |
| Chitra  |      80 |
| Divya   |      79 |
| Eshan   |      81 |
| Farhan  |      77 |
| Gokul   | **250** |


🤔 Do you notice something strange?

All students scored between 77 and 82, but one student has 250 marks.

Can an exam out of 100 have 250 marks? ❌ No.

So, 250 is an outlier because it is very different from the rest of the values.

