=========

Why Do We Find Outliers?

Outliers can happen because:

Someone entered the wrong number (typing mistake)
A machine or sensor made an error
A very unusual event happened
The data was recorded incorrectly

For example:

You sold 52 items, but someone accidentally typed:

520

Now 520 becomes an outlier.

===========

What Does IQR Do?

IQR acts like a teacher checking the class.

It looks at all the values and asks:

"Does this number look very different from the others?"

If the answer is Yes, it marks it as an outlier.

